WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.503
- A middle school student started firing two handguns in the middle of class.

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:06.131
- There's a teacher that's being called the hero this morning...

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:07.424
- Melo, what's up?

00:00:07.757 --> 00:00:09.134
- Have you seen this story on the news about

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:11.469
the shooting outside Indy? This dude's a hero.

00:00:11.761 --> 00:00:12.554
- Oh, for real?

00:00:12.554 --> 00:00:14.014
- I think you should go out there to check him out.

00:00:14.389 --> 00:00:15.807
- You think he wants all that attention?

00:00:15.807 --> 00:00:18.059
- Just let him know that you appreciate him—that's it.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.769
- You think he'd wanna watch a game with me?

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:49.090
- [Dispatch] Active shooter, Noblesville School. Active shooter, Noblesville School.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:54.888
Male, with a gun. The 1032 has a silencer on it. Second floor, second floor. 

00:00:54.929 --> 00:00:56.806
- [Police Officer 1] Dispatch, 7013, shooter is contained. 

00:00:56.973 --> 00:00:59.684
- [Police Officer 2] Dispatch, if you haven't notified other schools, lock them down.

00:00:59.768 --> 00:01:02.395
- [Police Officer 1] Shooter is in handcuffs, weapons are secured.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:08.234
- Jason Seaman. Teacher by day, football coach by night.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:12.197
On May 25th, 2018, he stopped a school shooting 

00:01:12.197 --> 00:01:13.948
in his seventh grade science class.

00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:18.203
- First off, as a person who isn't looking for attention,

00:01:18.203 --> 00:01:20.997
nor entirely comfortable with the situation I'm currently in

00:01:21.539 --> 00:01:26.294
- The scariest 15 seconds of his life became his 15 minutes of fame.

00:01:26.628 --> 00:01:29.464
- My actions on that day, uh, in my mind were the only acceptable

00:01:29.464 --> 00:01:32.300
actions I could have done given the circumstances.

00:01:32.383 --> 00:01:36.262
- A quick-thinking science teacher is being credited with saving lives.

00:01:36.513 --> 00:01:38.098
- Heroically confronting the student

00:01:38.139 --> 00:01:40.642
- Just about everybody who's ever met him has come out of the woodwork now

00:01:40.725 --> 00:01:43.895
- Ramey came up with the idea to start a GoFundMe page

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:47.023
- Serving as the honorary chairperson of the Indiana Derby

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:49.651
- Honored tonight at the Pacers' season opener

00:01:49.818 --> 00:01:51.778
- Gave Jason Seaman a new car

00:01:51.986 --> 00:01:55.990
- President Trump praising an Indiana teacher for stopping a school shooting

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:58.284
- Chicago Cubs invited Seaman to come up today

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.286
- Now has a beer named after him

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.705
- [chanting] Ja-son Sea-man!

00:02:02.705 --> 00:02:05.750
- Not one to seek the spotlight, today science teacher

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:09.337
Jason Seaman couldn't avoid being the center of attention in Noblesville.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:12.757
- Ever since, he's become the biggest hero in town.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:23.893
- Thank you. Appreciate that.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:31.401
That is the most awkward thing for me because I don't feel I did anything special.

00:02:31.401 --> 00:02:33.862
There was a kid and kids in need of help

00:02:33.862 --> 00:02:38.575
and to be told you're somebody special for helping a kid is absurd to me. 

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.662
That's not necessary, not at all.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.539
- Yeah, well it is to all of us.

00:02:44.789 --> 00:02:45.331
- Thank you.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:45.915
- You bet.

00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:49.502
- She just said that every time I come in here

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:52.297
everybody in here wants to pay for my meal. 

00:02:52.297 --> 00:02:56.217
So that's kinda crazy to think about cuz if I look around

00:02:56.217 --> 00:02:58.803
I see three or four faces I actually know. 

00:02:58.803 --> 00:03:01.389
I go to a restaurant expecting to pay for my own food

00:03:01.764 --> 00:03:04.684
wanting to pay for my own food, and they don't let me.

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:07.270
So that's, uh...that's weird. Very weird.

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:14.235
- Noblesville is a typical Midwest county seat. 

00:03:14.235 --> 00:03:17.113
We are in a very, very tough league.

00:03:17.113 --> 00:03:20.366
But they're doing well. We have a young coach. He's well-respected.

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:24.621
- Whenever they can get out here and just relax, they're at their best. 

00:03:24.621 --> 00:03:27.123
Cuz they have so much pressure and stress of being in middle school. 

00:03:27.123 --> 00:03:30.627
When they can put all that in the rearview and just have fun and play

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:32.754
they're all smiles. You can see it, and they're getting after it.

00:03:32.754 --> 00:03:35.423
- Whoever catches it gets a Gatorade on Monday.

00:03:38.009 --> 00:03:39.010
- [Cheering]

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:40.220
- Hey, got another one!

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:43.765
- I teach seventh-grade science at Noblesville West Middle School

00:03:43.765 --> 00:03:45.725
and I coach the eighth grade football team.

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:47.936
You guys are my smelliest friends.

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:48.645
- Really?

00:03:48.645 --> 00:03:49.187
- Yes. By far.

00:03:49.187 --> 00:03:50.271
- I'm your friend?

00:03:50.271 --> 00:03:52.482
- My smelliest friends, yes.

00:03:54.442 --> 00:03:57.320
- If you take my first year teaching, it was a rocky road.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.989
I was learning as I was going, and then I started to 

00:03:59.989 --> 00:04:03.868
develop my classroom personality, and that continues to change and evolve.

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:09.207
I try not to let the shooting affect it. Coaching—it definitely has.

00:04:09.707 --> 00:04:13.211
Cuz I always tried to keep, you know, this barrier between myself

00:04:13.211 --> 00:04:18.549
and the players, and I can definitely tell that this year, it's just different.

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:21.010
Noblesville has a lot of positives going for it.

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:24.472
Uh, just one dark cloud that's kinda still hovering a little bit.

00:04:25.723 --> 00:04:27.141
- Is this really who we want to be?

00:04:27.141 --> 00:04:32.146
A country where anybody at any time could be shot to death?

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:35.525
- It's happened again, uh, here in the United States—a school shooting.

00:04:35.525 --> 00:04:36.776
- One student has been injured

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:37.819
- Two students were shot

00:04:37.819 --> 00:04:38.736
- Gunshot wounds

00:04:38.736 --> 00:04:40.154
- Two 15-year-olds dead

00:04:41.823 --> 00:04:44.492
- The bullet came from a room attached to his dorm room

00:04:44.492 --> 00:04:46.244
- Fired a gun in his classroom

00:04:46.244 --> 00:04:48.454
- There have been 23 school shootings 

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:51.582
where someone was hurt or killed so far this year

00:04:51.582 --> 00:04:52.834
- Wake Forest University

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:53.751
- Lincoln High School

00:04:53.751 --> 00:04:54.877
- Santa Fe High School

00:04:54.877 --> 00:04:56.087
- Huffman High School

00:04:56.087 --> 00:04:57.046
- Italy High School 

00:04:57.046 --> 00:04:58.256
- [Stoneman] Douglas High School

00:04:58.402 --> 00:04:59.651
- Forest High School

00:04:59.651 --> 00:05:01.613
- The list goes on and on and on

00:05:02.198 --> 00:05:03.658
- And it wasn't even June yet.

00:05:04.387 --> 00:05:07.640
- Of course you know of all the shootings. I mean, we hear 'em.

00:05:08.016 --> 00:05:11.894
And you just, you know, think it's not gonna happen in little ol' Noblesville.

00:05:11.894 --> 00:05:12.812
Well, it did.

00:05:13.062 --> 00:05:13.980
- We have breaking news

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.398
- Breaking news from Indiana now

00:05:15.398 --> 00:05:17.233
- Another school shooting this morning

00:05:17.233 --> 00:05:18.985
- Take a deep breath with me on this one.

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:20.820
We have breaking news in the state of Indiana.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:24.991
There has been a shooting at Noblesville West Middle School. 

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:27.577
- It was just one of those days where people are gonna show up

00:05:27.577 --> 00:05:28.953
and we were gonna take the test

00:05:29.245 --> 00:05:31.331
and that would be that, and we'd go into the weekend.

00:05:31.789 --> 00:05:35.043
And first hour went by fine, and second hour is when everything went down.

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:38.379
- The preliminary information is that a male student 

00:05:38.379 --> 00:05:40.298
asked to be excused from his class.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:44.719
- He left to use the restroom. And he came back.

00:05:44.719 --> 00:05:47.180
And my friend opened the door for him.

00:05:47.263 --> 00:05:49.390
- He didn't come in for a solid 10 seconds.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:52.060
And then as soon as he came in, shots were fired.

00:05:52.643 --> 00:05:55.188
- The seventh-grader was armed with a pair of handguns.

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:57.607
He did shoot the teacher in the process as well as 

00:05:57.607 --> 00:06:00.026
a female student who is in critical condition.

00:06:00.818 --> 00:06:02.320
- I saw Ella hit the floor, and, like, it all happened in slow motion.

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:06.532
And, like, nobody was standing- or like, getting down.

00:06:06.991 --> 00:06:08.826
- The first sign that something was off was

00:06:08.826 --> 00:06:12.538
the pressure I felt in my abdomen, um—which was the first bullet.

00:06:12.955 --> 00:06:15.083
And that's when I saw—we just made eye contact

00:06:15.083 --> 00:06:16.793
and he was pointing his weapon straight at me. 

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:20.046
That's kind of where it just clicked.

00:06:20.671 --> 00:06:23.216
And I acted. I had a basketball in my hand.

00:06:23.299 --> 00:06:25.051
I reared back and I threw it. I threw it at him. 

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:29.514
And it made him have to move, and that changed his aim point.

00:06:29.972 --> 00:06:33.559
And then I just tackled him to the ground and told my students to get outta there.

00:06:33.893 --> 00:06:35.395
- We all, like, got up super quick.

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:37.897
I think at that time, really reality kicked in for me.

00:06:38.022 --> 00:06:41.025
- We're now learning how quickly the situation was contained. 

00:06:41.275 --> 00:06:46.197
- Authorities swarming the scene, students escorted on buses out to safety.

00:06:46.364 --> 00:06:48.825
- (Dispatch) All units seen as safe. Shooter is handcuffed.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:52.495
- Virtually all school shootings occur in under five minutes.

00:06:52.662 --> 00:06:56.916
To get there this quick and to get it stopped and get him identified and down 

00:06:57.291 --> 00:06:58.459
clearly saved lives.

00:07:03.381 --> 00:07:08.094
- Jason was a defensive lineman in an Illinois college. Big guy.

00:07:08.302 --> 00:07:14.016
You know, because of that, perhaps, it was more instinctive to just tackle this kid

00:07:14.016 --> 00:07:16.769
you know, and get him down. And obviously he did that.

00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:20.022
- I don't know if it's the product of being in contact sports.

00:07:20.022 --> 00:07:22.275
I mean, I was in wrestling. I was in football.

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:24.652
Basketball, the way I played it, was a contact sport.

00:07:25.153 --> 00:07:29.115
I don't know. I've just always been a reactive person.

00:07:29.115 --> 00:07:33.119
I don't know. I didn't think about it. I didn't make a choice. It was just what I did.

00:07:33.494 --> 00:07:34.704
I'm a person of action.

00:07:34.704 --> 00:07:35.997
[Shouting] I know you can run harder than that—

00:07:35.997 --> 00:07:39.167
I know you can! I know you can run harder than that!

00:07:40.126 --> 00:07:43.254
- It's easy to say that you would put yourself out there

00:07:43.254 --> 00:07:45.465
and protect a kid, but it's another thing to do it. 

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:47.967
- He put his life out to save others.

00:07:48.176 --> 00:07:52.138
- Even after being shot, he still came back and did football with us.

00:07:52.305 --> 00:07:55.183
- He's really open, and he's just, like, a great person.

00:07:55.391 --> 00:07:57.310
It's just amazing what Coach Seaman did

00:07:57.435 --> 00:07:59.187
- An amazing coach and an amazing person.

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:02.315
- He's just a good guy, and I appreciate him being my coach.

00:08:02.482 --> 00:08:03.733
- Yes, I think he's a hero

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:08.738
- Hero is always a weird word for me. I think any time a situation is intense

00:08:08.738 --> 00:08:10.615
and a good person does the right thing

00:08:11.616 --> 00:08:14.076
they don't feel like they should be recognized for it because 

00:08:14.118 --> 00:08:15.244
they were just doing the right thing.

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:19.665
- Jason is a humble hero. He doesn't want the spotlight. 

00:08:20.249 --> 00:08:21.250
But let's be real. 

00:08:21.751 --> 00:08:23.127
He took three bullets. 

00:08:23.878 --> 00:08:26.839
His student, Ella Whistler, took seven.

00:08:27.381 --> 00:08:29.342
Both of them are already back at school

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:31.385
with bullets still in their bodies.

00:08:32.428 --> 00:08:34.889
- I had Ella all year. She's a showman at heart.

00:08:34.889 --> 00:08:38.392
She loves to sing. She loves to dance. She loves to just have fun in that regard. 

00:08:38.893 --> 00:08:41.604
I think that was one of the hardest parts, for me.

00:08:41.979 --> 00:08:45.233
Cuz I knew about her injuries, and I wondered if she'd get back to that.

00:08:46.234 --> 00:08:49.403
- The clavicle was shattered, her first-second rib was fractured

00:08:49.403 --> 00:08:52.281
and her C5 and C6 was fractured. 

00:08:52.281 --> 00:08:56.452
So it all affected the nerve damage on her whole right arm.

00:08:56.494 --> 00:08:59.872
- My physical therapist is, like, working on my shoulder cuz all my muscles

00:08:59.872 --> 00:09:01.874
are tight and so they're trying to loosen them up.

00:09:02.124 --> 00:09:06.546
And the occupational's working on my hand and arm, trying to get my arms 

00:09:06.546 --> 00:09:10.216
straight and my hand back to 100 percent function.

00:09:10.216 --> 00:09:13.469
There's a chance that my hand won't get back to 100 percent.

00:09:13.469 --> 00:09:15.805
- Yeah. You remember what else we're always worried about.

00:09:15.805 --> 00:09:20.017
Cuz the bullet moved. The bullet moved closer to your spinal cord.

00:09:21.018 --> 00:09:24.772
- I mean, the debate on firearms is always going to rage on

00:09:24.772 --> 00:09:27.233
because it's a personal opinion. And when

00:09:27.275 --> 00:09:30.570
people get into personal opinions, there's never a winner. 

00:09:30.611 --> 00:09:33.948
There's no common ground because everybody wants to win. 

00:09:34.198 --> 00:09:38.995
Do I think putting more guns in the school will help solve the problem? Probably not.

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:41.497
I've only experienced what happened to me.

00:09:41.747 --> 00:09:45.376
I think we have to treat each other better if we really wanna get

00:09:45.376 --> 00:09:49.380
at the heart of the problem. And that is a whole different ballgame. 

00:09:51.882 --> 00:09:54.885
- We are here tonight to pay tribute to the many who have gave

00:09:54.885 --> 00:09:58.681
selflessly on May 25 and the following weeks.

00:09:59.223 --> 00:10:05.479
Today, Noblesville says thank you to all of our heroes, big and small.

00:10:05.479 --> 00:10:13.326
[Applause]

00:10:13.821 --> 00:10:15.531
- [Chanting] One, two, three, FAMILY!

00:10:15.531 --> 00:10:18.938
[Cheering]

00:10:22.288 --> 00:10:26.250
- Nothin' is gonna light a fire faster than a big return.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:29.795
OK? A big return. We worked on it yesterday. 

00:10:29.837 --> 00:10:34.383
Whoever catches it, everybody else get in front of him and block like crazy.

00:10:34.592 --> 00:10:37.428
Let's score points on the first play of this game.

00:10:37.428 --> 00:10:41.974
First play. Block for each other, run, hit everybody, have fun.

00:10:42.183 --> 00:10:44.435
Return on three. [All] One, two, three, RETURN!

00:10:45.269 --> 00:10:50.316
With everything that's happened, we are the family that sports brings together.

00:10:50.483 --> 00:10:54.904
On the field, we like having fun. Off the field, stuff happens

00:10:54.904 --> 00:10:56.030
and it brings you together.

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:59.742
So we always try to look out for each other instead of letting it divide us.

00:11:03.371 --> 00:11:08.209
I want to be known in the community as a teacher, as a coach, as a father.

00:11:08.209 --> 00:11:09.877
I want to be known as that person. 

00:11:10.336 --> 00:11:12.630
I didn't need to get shot for that to happen. 

00:11:13.005 --> 00:11:16.842
I'm moving forward. This year's begun. I've got a great group of kids.

00:11:16.842 --> 00:11:20.179
The trust is there. I know some teachers—they're still struggling with it

00:11:20.179 --> 00:11:24.725
but it's a chapter of my story now. And it won't be separated

00:11:24.725 --> 00:11:26.227
as much as I would want to be.

00:11:26.644 --> 00:11:31.315
I'm just gonna continue to do my job the best I can and, you know

00:11:31.357 --> 00:11:33.109
everything else will take care of itself. 

00:11:37.238 --> 00:11:39.407
- [Child] It's the cow!

00:11:39.949 --> 00:11:42.493
- That is the cow. Can't see it from here.

00:11:49.166 --> 00:11:51.001
Oh my goodness! No way.

00:11:51.001 --> 00:11:52.002
- What's goin' on?

00:11:52.002 --> 00:11:54.755
- No way. How are you?

00:11:54.755 --> 00:11:55.673
- All good.

00:11:55.673 --> 00:11:59.009
- I have been set up. Man, come on in, come on in.

00:12:01.303 --> 00:12:03.931
- I heard about the story, and it definitely takes

00:12:03.931 --> 00:12:08.102
a lotta heart and a lotta, I mean, you sacrificed. Most definitely.

00:12:08.102 --> 00:12:11.814
So I just wanted to come and, you know, show a little appreciation for that.

00:12:12.106 --> 00:12:14.692
- I'm floored right now. Can't believe you'd take the time out to do this. 

00:12:14.859 --> 00:12:15.484
- Yeah, man.

00:12:15.568 --> 00:12:20.239
- Can you say hi, Jameson? He plays football. You think you can tackle him?

00:12:21.991 --> 00:12:25.110
[Laughing]

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:25.797
- He waited till I turned around.

00:12:27.079 --> 00:12:27.904
Is this Tennessee?

00:12:28.007 --> 00:12:30.286
Tennessee, Auburn and Florida, yeah.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.460
When did you start playing football?

00:12:33.127 --> 00:12:36.172
- I started playing football...my sister

00:12:36.172 --> 00:12:39.884
took me to the park in third grade, and I wasn't good at all.

00:12:40.176 --> 00:12:40.468
- No?

00:12:40.468 --> 00:12:41.635
- Yeah, I was...

00:12:41.635 --> 00:12:42.094
- Didn't work?

00:12:42.219 --> 00:12:43.679
- Nah, I was playing, like, left guard.

00:12:43.679 --> 00:12:47.558
I was just like the kid you just throw out there, like, here's your jersey and--

00:12:47.558 --> 00:12:48.350
- Just gettin' in the way a little bit

00:12:48.350 --> 00:12:49.351
- Yeah.

00:12:50.603 --> 00:12:52.438
- How many plays do they usually bring into the huddle?

00:12:52.938 --> 00:12:55.858
- Well, you know our quarterback's pretty good. 

00:12:55.858 --> 00:12:58.110
- Yeah, that's why I'm wondering. 

00:12:58.360 --> 00:13:01.071
- So, our playbook is crazy. And Sean'll be like, I see it.

00:13:01.071 --> 00:13:03.949
I had a dream about it, like, "I see it. It's gonna happen just like this."

00:13:03.991 --> 00:13:04.784
- He's got visions.

00:13:04.784 --> 00:13:06.368
- And then on Sunday when it happens just like that

00:13:06.368 --> 00:13:08.746
you be like, "Man, this dude. He's really smart."

00:13:09.079 --> 00:13:13.542
That's why I like playing offense. It's like, defense, is so—you gotta anticipate so much.

00:13:13.542 --> 00:13:14.001
- Mhmm.

00:13:14.001 --> 00:13:17.671
- Offense is more, like, you gotta anticipate a little bit to a certain extent

00:13:17.671 --> 00:13:17.713
- Offense is more, like, you gotta anticipate a little bit to a certain extent
just based off coverage and stuff, but shoot, you always kinda, like, got the one-up.

00:13:17.713 --> 00:13:21.550
just based off coverage and stuff, but shoot, you always kinda, like, got the one-up.

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:22.676
- You got that control.

00:13:22.676 --> 00:13:23.719
- Yeah, you got control.

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:27.139
- So you're a celebrity in this town now.

00:13:27.598 --> 00:13:28.599
- In this town is the key word.

00:13:28.599 --> 00:13:29.058
- [Laughing]

00:13:29.058 --> 00:13:29.558
